**user**:
> Is there a way in facet_grid to make one row narrower (less tall) than the others, even though it covers the same span of values?
**assistant**:
> Not with base `facet_grid()` alone: panel row heights are either equal or determined by free scale ranges via `space = "free_y"`.
> 
> For explicit relative heights, use **forcepanelsizes**:
> 
> ```r
> library(ggplot2)
> library(forcepanelsizes)
> 
> p <- ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) +
>   geom_point() +
>   facet_grid(row.facet ~ ., scales = "free_y")
> 
> force_panelsizes(
>   p,
>   rows = c(1, 3, 3)   # first facet row is one-third as tall
> )
> ```
> 
> The values are relative heights, in the displayed facet-row order. For exact grid units:
> 
> ```r
> force_panelsizes(p, rows = grid::unit(c(1, 3, 3), "null"))
> ```
> 
> If you need panel height to reflect the data range automatically, use:
> 
> ```r
> facet_grid(row.facet ~ ., scales = "free_y", space = "free_y")
> ```
> 
> —but that will not shrink a row whose y-span is identical to the others.
